{"_id":"never-stop-blowing-up-rules","name":"Never Stop Blowing Up - Rules","type":"JournalEntry","img":"icons/svg/book.svg","system":{},"pages":[{"_id":"overview","name":"Game Rules","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h1>Never Stop Blowing Up - Game Rules</h1><p>Welcome to Never Stop Blowing Up, the explosive tabletop RPG where action never stops!</p><h2>Quick Access</h2><p><strong>Digital Rulebook PDF:</strong> <a href=\"/assets/Never_Stop_Blowing_Up_Rules.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Open Full Rules PDF</a></p><p><em>Right-click the link above and select \"Open in New Tab\" or \"Save Link As\" to download the complete rulebook.</em></p><h1>How to Play</h1><h2>Starting the Game</h2><h3>Build your character choosing:</h3><ul><li><strong>An Action Hero Name</strong></li><li><strong>A Catchphrase</strong></li><li><strong>Three Abilities</strong></li></ul><h2>Character Skills</h2><h3>You have 9 key skills.</h3><ul><li><strong>Stunts:</strong> Parkour, climbing, acrobatics, speed</li><li><strong>Brawl:</strong> Hand-to-hand combat, physical confrontation</li><li><strong>Tough:</strong> Endurance, resistance, survival, willpower</li><li><strong>Tech:</strong> Computer systems, digital security, technology</li><li><strong>Weapons:</strong> Firearms, melee weapons, ranged combat</li><li><strong>Drive:</strong> Vehicle operation, chases, piloting</li><li><strong>Sneak:</strong> Stealth, infiltration, subterfuge</li><li><strong>Wits:</strong> Investigation, knowledge, problem-solving</li><li><strong>Hot:</strong> Social interaction, charm, persuasion, charisma</li></ul><h3>Each skill starts at a d4.</h3><h2>Blowing Up</h2><p>Every time an action hero gets the highest value on their die, it <strong>\"blows up\"</strong> and that skill moves up to the next die type.</p><p>Roll that new die and add the results to the current check.</p><p>If that new roll is also the highest value, the skill continues to <strong>blow up.</strong></p><p>Repeat this process until you reach a d20.</p><h3>Example:</h3><ul><li>You roll a d6 for a Weapons check</li><li>You roll a 6  The 6 counts, roll again!</li><li>You roll another 6  Now you have 12, roll again!</li><li>You roll a 3  Final result is 15 (6+6+3)</li></ul><p>This explosive mechanic creates unpredictable, escalating action that defines the \"Never Stop Blowing Up\" experience!</p><h2>Prepared Actions</h2><p>When an Action Hero has time to prepare for a skill check and is not under stress, they can use a <strong>prepared action</strong>. Instead of rolling a die, they take half the die value for that stat.</p><h2>Turbo Tokens</h2><p>When an Action Hero fails a check they get a <strong>Turbo Token</strong>, which can be spent one-to-one to increase the value of a die roll.</p><p>If a die roll is increased to its highest value, it triggers a blow up as if the highest value had been rolled. Spent <strong>Turbo Tokens</strong> are placed on a player-specific tray in front of the board.</p><p>If both characters are in the same scene, players can spend <strong>Turbo Tokens</strong> for friends, but at 2x cost.</p><h3>Example:</h3><ul><li>You have 3 <strong>Turbo Tokens</strong></li><li>You roll a d6 for a Weapons check</li><li>You roll a 5  You add 1 <strong>Turbo Token</strong> to the roll, making it a 6 and trigger it to <strong>Blow Up</strong>.</li><li>You now roll a d8  Getting a 6. You add your remaining 2 <strong>Turbo Tokens</strong> to the roll, blowing it up again!</li><li>You now roll a d10, getting a 3  Final result is 17 (6+8+3).</li></ul><h2>Injury</h2><p>There are three injury levels.</p><ul><li><strong>Superficial</strong></li><li><strong>Severe</strong></li><li><strong>Adrenalized</strong></li></ul><p>When an Action Hero fails a <strong>Tough Check</strong> by 5 or more, they take an <strong>Injury Level</strong>.</p><p>At <strong>Severe Injury</strong>, players must spend double the amount of <strong>Turbo Tokens</strong> (i.e., 2 Turbo Tokens to Blow Up a 5 on a d6).</p><p>At the <strong>Adrenalized</strong> injury level, the injured character receives 10 <strong>Turbo Tokens</strong>.</p><p>When an Adrenalized character fails a <strong>Tough Check</strong>, they become either <strong>Incapacitated</strong> or <strong>Dead</strong>, depending on the attacker's intention.</p><h2>Quick Play Tips</h2><ol><li><strong>Start Small:</strong> Begin with d4 or d6 dice and work your way up</li><li><strong>Embrace Explosions:</strong> When dice explode, lean into the chaos and escalation</li><li><strong>Use Turbo Tokens Wisely:</strong> Save them for crucial moments or dramatic reveals</li><li><strong>Work as a Team:</strong> Group abilities are powerful when coordinated</li><li><strong>Keep it Moving:</strong> The game thrives on momentum and escalating action</li></ol><h2>Difficulty Classes</h2><ul><li><strong>Easy:</strong> DC 5-8</li><li><strong>Moderate:</strong> DC 9-12</li><li><strong>Hard:</strong> DC 13-16</li><li><strong>Very Hard:</strong> DC 17-20</li><li><strong>Nearly Impossible:</strong> DC 21+</li></ul><h1>Abilities</h1><p>At the end of each session, players may use remaining <strong>Turbo Tokens</strong> to purchase extra abilities. Individual abilities cost 2 Turbo Tokens.</p><ul><li><strong>By the Book:</strong> Lower the DC of a Hot Check by 3 when interacting with authority figures</li><li><strong>Burglar:</strong> Lower the DC of a Sneak Check by 3 when entering a protected location</li><li><strong>Connected:</strong> Lower the DC of a Hot Check by 3 when searching for a helpful ally</li><li><strong>Demolitions:</strong> Lower the DC of a Tech Check by 3 when explosives are involved</li><li><strong>Duelist:</strong> Lower the DC of a Weapons Check by 3 against someone wielding the same weapon</li><li><strong>Escape Artist:</strong> Lower the DC of a Sneak Check by 3 when escaping restraints or imprisonment</li><li><strong>Flashy:</strong> Lower the DC of a Hot Check by 5 if it's the first roll after you've Blown Up</li><li><strong>Grit:</strong> Lower the DC of a Tough Check by 3 when resisting a Brawl Check</li><li><strong>Hacker:</strong> Lower the DC of a Tech Check by 3 when breaking into a computer database</li><li><strong>Hotwire:</strong> When interacting with vehicles, use Drive instead of Tech</li><li><strong>Inspiring:</strong> Each time you succeed at a check, an ally of your choice receives 1 Turbo Token</li><li><strong>Interrogator:</strong> Lower the DC of a Wits Check by 3 to draw information out of an opponent</li><li><strong>Leap of Faith:</strong> Lower the DC of a Stunts Check by 3 when making a jump that could injure you</li><li><strong>Loyal:</strong> Your Turbo Tokens give friends +1 at a one-to-one rate</li><li><strong>Lucky:</strong> Spend 2 Turbo Tokens to reroll any check <em>(Once Per Episode)</em></li><li><strong>Martial Artist:</strong> Spend a Turbo Token to force an enemy to resist your Brawl with Wits instead of Tough</li><li><strong>Menacing:</strong> Use Brawl instead of Hot when intimidating an NPC</li><li><strong>Nerves of Steel:</strong> Spend a Turbo Token to treat a snap decision as a Prepared Action</li><li><strong>Poker Face:</strong> When attempting to conceal the truth, use Tough instead of Hot</li><li><strong>Prepared:</strong> Spend 2 Turbo Tokens to just happen to have one commonplace item with you <em>(GM's Discretion)</em></li><li><strong>Protector:</strong> Lower the DC of a check by 3 when defending your friends</li><li><strong>Quick Healing:</strong> Recover one injury level at the end of an encounter</li><li><strong>Relentless:</strong> Gain 2 Turbo Tokens when you fail a check</li><li><strong>Resilient:</strong> Turbo Tokens are worth double when used to boost against an attack that targets you</li><li><strong>Skilled:</strong> Increase your die type for one skill by 1 for the purposes of halving</li><li><strong>Smokin':</strong> Lower the DC of a Hot Check by 3 when making a first impression</li><li><strong>Stealthy:</strong> Lower the DC of a Sneak Check by 3 when trying to avoid being seen</li><li><strong>Trained:</strong> -1 to DCs for a Stat of your choice</li><li><strong>Studied:</strong> <em>(Replaces Trained)</em> -3 to DCs for Stat of your choice</li><li><strong>Mastery:</strong> <em>(Replaces Studied)</em> -5 to DCs for a Stat of your choice</li><li><strong>Transporter:</strong> Lower the DC of a Drive Check by 3 to avoid pursuers</li><li><strong>Trouble Maker:</strong> Spend a Turbo Token to locate and receive help from a criminal network <em>(GM's Discretion)</em></li><li><strong>Wealthy:</strong> Spend a Turbo Token to ease a bad situation with cash</li><li><strong>Wild Card:</strong> You are a Wild Card</li></ul><h1>Group Suites</h1><p>New 'group suites' of abilities are unlocked for purchase once all players reach a higher die type (i.e., one d6 from every player). Abilities from group suites cost 10 turbo tokens for an individual, or 18 for the entire group.</p><ul><li><strong>Criminal Conspiracy (d6):</strong> Heists, cons, and criminal operations  <ul>  <li><strong>Hot:</strong> Roll Hot in response to the first attack of an encounter to dissuade an opponent.</li>  <li><strong>Item:</strong> When in a new location, produce a single useful item.</li>  <li><strong>Tech:</strong> Once per episode, add your Tech Die to a Sneak Die.</li>  </ul></li><li><strong>La Familia (d6):</strong> Family bonds and mutual support  <ul>  <li><strong>Skill Die:</strong> Lend a teammate a skill die.</li>  <li><strong>Tokens:</strong> Spend tokens for other people at a 1:1 exchange rate.</li>  <li><strong>Tough:</strong> Roll Tough on someone else's behalf.</li>  </ul></li><li><strong>Diesel Circus (d8):</strong> Vehicle-based mayhem and stunts  <ul>  <li><strong>Double Explosion:</strong> Doubles your amount of tokens.</li>  <li><strong>Drive Check:</strong> On a successful Drive Check, make another skill check.</li>  <li><strong>Injury Advantage:</strong> Roll twice on the first roll after an injury.</li>  </ul></li><li><strong>Tactical Command (d8):</strong> Military precision and coordination  <ul>  <li><strong>Reroll:</strong> Reroll on a failure.</li>  <li><strong>Shared Tokens:</strong> Spend Turbo Tokens across scenes.</li>  <li><strong>Token Gain:</strong> Characters gain a Turbo Token at the end of a scene where they have zero.</li>  </ul></li><li><strong>Alpha Squad (d10):</strong> Elite team operations  <ul>  <li><strong>Group Explosion:</strong> In a scene where everyone uses a different skill, reduce the range to Blow Up by 1.</li>  <li><strong>Skill Add:</strong> Two people roll the same skill and add the totals together.</li>  <li><strong>Suit Up:</strong> The group may 'suit up' and each take 2 Turbo Tokens.</li>  </ul></li><li><strong>Marauders (d10):</strong> Destructive force and chaos  <ul>  <li><strong>+10:</strong> Beating an opponent by more than 10 means you defeat an additional opponent.</li>  <li><strong>Destroyer:</strong> Gain a Turbo Token on any turn where you destroy an object.</li>  <li><strong>Firestarter:</strong> Start a fire, short circuit electronics, or dissolve a structure as part of any action.</li>  </ul></li><li><strong>The Continentals (d12):</strong> Sophisticated espionage  <ul>  <li><strong>Hot Checks:</strong> Two successful Hot Checks auto-succeeds on stealing from an opponent.</li>  <li><strong>Melee:</strong> Lower the DC of a Weapons Checks using melee weapons.</li>  <li><strong>Wits:</strong> Turbo Tokens for Wits help increase the die type.</li>  </ul></li><li><strong>The Ones (d12):</strong> Peak performance and excellence  <ul>  <li><strong>Max Roll:</strong> Treat a Nat 1 as a max die roll.</li>  <li><strong>Reroll:</strong> Reroll a failure with a different skill.</li>  <li><strong>Turbo Tokens:</strong> Accept a Nat 1 to gain half the Turbo Tokens of the die value.</li>  </ul></li><li><strong>Bustin' Makes Me Feel Good (d20):</strong> Supernatural encounters  <ul>  <li><strong>GM:</strong> Become the GM for 60 seconds.</li>  <li><strong>Group Explosion:</strong> Everybody else at the table graduates all of their lowest die type up by one.</li>  <li><strong>Track Restart:</strong> Restart that skill track, now rolling a second die and taking the better result.</li>  </ul></li></ul><h2>Compendiums Available</h2><ul><li><strong>Player Abilities:</strong> Individual character abilities</li><li><strong>Group Abilities:</strong> Team-based powers</li><li><strong>Rules Reference:</strong> Journal with quick rules and full PDF access</li></ul><hr><p><strong>For complete rules, character creation, and advanced mechanics, see the full PDF rulebook linked above.</strong></p>"},"image":{},"video":{},"src":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"never-stop-blowing-up","systemVersion":"1.0.0","coreVersion":"12.343","createdTime":1757447867325,"modifiedTime":1757447867325,"lastModifiedBy":"foundryUser"}}